+
+# 2026-10-14-codex-priority-observation
+
+English | [中文](2026-10-14-codex-priority-observation.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Adds optional priority serviceTier to durable request controls and bounded responseServiceTier observations to successful compact Assistant finish chunks. Priority capability is exact-model metadata and is opt-in; no default, global setting, or event type is added.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Declaration](#declaration)
+- [Compatibility](#compatibility)
+- [Verification](#verification)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+<a id="declaration"></a>
+## Declaration
+
+```yaml persistence-change
+schemaVersion: 1
+id: 2026-10-14-codex-priority-observation
+baseline: false
+changes:
+  - root: "event:assistant/attempt"
+    previous: "2026-09-16-session-format-v4"
+    after: "37ba606d1e04fae7c049b3f199f80a5a338dc227fb95041af33cb10f95b19eb4"
+    decision: same-version
+  - root: "event:assistant/message"
+    previous: "2026-09-16-session-format-v4"
+    after: "4919a3d40fa2af7e33f63bc5cb8f8ff612b18f6246527abf0e11386c0e4d323a"
+    decision: same-version
+  - root: "event:request/header"
+    previous: "2026-09-16-session-format-v4"
+    after: "fcdea6a5a9acc421c24067202095b6ab4f8804bb6c57d0a1fbf420934277695c"
+    decision: same-version
+```
+
+<a id="compatibility"></a>
+## Compatibility
+
+Same-version additive fields: current readers accept existing headers and streams with both fields absent. Priority is scheduling intent, not a content, route, reasoning or tool-history discriminator. Previous readers ignore the optional observation and request control, preserving content and route interpretation but not priority scheduling; do not resume these sessions on an older Host if priority intent must be retained. New readers reject malformed tier controls and response observations; errors and cancellations never carry an observation. Finalized format-4 records and historical schemas remain unchanged.
+
+<a id="verification"></a>
+## Verification
+
+Actual installed pi-ai streamSimple SSE fixtures and real Cordis Loader composition pass: priority reaches the request body through onPayload; raw terminal done/completed/incomplete tiers differ from requested tiers; absent/malformed/failed observations remain absent. Prepared-call generation, one-shot equality, unsupported pre-I/O validation, durable header restoration and compact observation tests pass. Focused service-tier suites: 26 tests passed. A fresh loop restores same-route serviceTier without a selector rerun; core logic only adds this seed inheritance. No real provider calls or dependency changes.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+## Dev Note
+
+None.
