+
+`LlmCallControls.serviceTier` and `GenerateOptions.serviceTier` accept only `'priority'`. Omission preserves provider defaults; `LlmResolvedModelInfo.serviceTiers` declares exact-route support, and absent support rejects an explicit tier with `UNSUPPORTED_SERVICE_TIER` before provider I/O. Prepared calls freeze this control and configuration equality includes it. Request waterfalls can select it without changing Agent defaults. Successful terminal `finish` chunks may carry `responseServiceTier`, the observed response value rather than the requested value. It is a scalar matching `/^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$/`; unknown observations and failed finishes omit it. Existing compact Assistant streams preserve it, and their validating readers reject malformed observations.
 
 ### What you can do
 
